{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they brought him up from the pit.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: from within distress, exaltation; from within darkness, light; from within the degradation of the righteous, leadership, as it is said (Proverbs 30): ״אם נבלת בהתנשא״ — 'if you have been degraded, you will be exalted.' For thus we find in Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, who were raised up from within degradation, as it is said (Daniel 3): ״כפתו בסרבליהון פטישיהון וכרבלתהון ולבושיהון ורמיו לגוא אתון נורא יקידתא,״ and it is written: ״באדין מלכא הצלח לשדרך מישך ועבד נגו.״ Daniel was cast into the lions' pit and was saved and raised up, as it is said (Daniel 6): ״ודניאל דנא הצלח במלכות דריוש.״ Of Mordecai it is written (Esther 4): ״וילבש שק ואפר,״ and he was raised up, as it is said (Esther 8): ״ומרדכי יצא מלפני המלך בלבוש מלכות״ etc. So too here, in the case of Joseph: ״ויריצוהו מן הבור ויגלח ויחלף שמלותיו,״ and it is written (Ecclesiastes 4): ״כי מבית הסורים יצא למלוך.״ And so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted the verse (Exodus 1): ״ועלה מן הארץ״ — from within descent, ascent."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:16.434185629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}